    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n11 Acres Plus Derelict Cottage Share of Commonage\n\nA Little Piece of Heaven on Earth\n\nDernish Island is located 500m off the mainland of Co. Sligo and is uninhabited at present. It has stunning backdrops on all sides, with Donegal Bay and the Atlantic Ocean to the north and west, and majestic Benbulben and the North Sligo landscape to the east and south. On clear days, the Donegal Mountains and Slieve Liag cliffs can be seen.\n\nThe island can be accessed by boat from Milk Harbour, subject to making your own arrangements, or on foot or by jeep across Streedagh Beach when the tide is out. The island is approached on the south side and has one grass laneway travelling south to north through the centre of the island.\n\nThe subject property for sale is in two main lots (redlined), east and west of the access lane. The western lot comprises 5 acres of agricultural land and a derelict cottage. The eastern lot comprises 6 acres of agricultural land. In addition, there are two lots of sand dune commonage (yellowlined) on the north and east sides, extending to approximately 22 acres, with six shareholders in total.\n\nLot 1 Western Lot\n\nThe cottage on the 5-acre plot has been unoccupied since the mid-1950s and, unfortunately, has fallen into dereliction. However, it has potential for a marvellous renovation project for those seeking a challenge. The 5 acres are spread across four fields with low stone wall divides.\n\nLot 2 Eastern Lot\n\nThe 6 acres are spread across seven adjoining fields with small stone wall divides.\n\nDernish Island is a wildlife haven for flora and fauna, and when in season in April and May, it is a sea of bluebells, reflecting the colour of the ocean. Birdsong is ever present. The land on the island is still farmed, and a new owner of this land could get involved in various types of farming.\n\nIsland life is challenging and not for the faint-hearted, but a new owner seeking peace and solitude will rarely find such a suitable location.\n\nViewing arrangements and other details are available from REA McCarrick Sons.\n\nTel: 071 91 85050\nEmail: info@reamccarrick.ie\n\n"
      }
    ],
